{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Now I know that my strength was from You in my health, for at the time You hid Your face I was dismayed. Rabbi Moses said: for You set the meaning — You set me upon mountains of strength, like 'that glory may sing to You,' which is my glory. And others said: for the yod in להררי is the sign of the noun-marker, and the sense is 'to set him,' like הר. And Rabbi Judah HaLevi said: להררי is like 'mountains of the field' (Jeremiah 17:3), for the patterns of nouns vary."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:59.594480646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}